# Playwright BDD Architecture

When editing files under playwrightBDD/:

1. Features describe behaviour in Gherkin — no locators or implementation
2. Steps are thin glue — call page object methods only
3. Page objects own all locators, actions, and assertions
4. Fixtures in steps/steps.ts provide one page object per test (parallel-safe)
5. Never put locators in step definition files
6. Gherkin parameters are function args after the fixtures object
7. Run bddgen after changing features; run yarn test to verify
